response:
The graphs of \( y = f(x) = x^2 + 2bx + 1 \) and \( y = g(x) = 2a(x + b) \) do not intersect when the equation \( x^2 + 2bx + 1 = 2a(x + b) \) has no real solutions. Rearranging gives \( x^2 + (2b - 2a)x + (1 - 2ab) = 0 \). The discriminant must be negative: \( (2b - 2a)^2 - 4(1 - 2ab) < 0 \), which simplifies to \( a^2 + b^2 < 1 \). This is the interior of a unit circle, so the area is \( \pi \).
